{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Greater</b> — Japheth said: For the First Temple stood four hundred and ten years, and the Second Temple stood four hundred and twenty, which was in the days of Herodus, as he wrote in the book of Joseph son of Gorion. And Rabbi Moses said: For this was conditional — if they had been perfectly righteous, as Zechariah said: \"And it shall be, if you hearken to hear\" (Zechariah 6:15)."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved the epithet 'Japheth' to the Karaite exegete; 'Rabbi Moses' likely refers to Ibn Ezra's contemporary or a known rabbinic figure, left untranslated as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:30.344124394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}